# Cherry Tomato Pasta Sauce

A simple, fast pasta sauce made from fresh cherry tomatoes. Light, slightly sweet, and naturally emulsified with pasta water for a silky finish.

Yield: 2–3 servings  
Prep Time: 5 minutes  
Cook Time: 10–12 minutes  
Total Time: 15–17 minutes  

## Ingredients

- 3 cups cherry tomatoes  
- 2–3 tbsp olive oil  
- 3 cloves garlic, thinly sliced  
- 1/2 tsp salt (adjust to taste)  
- 1/4 tsp black pepper  
- Pinch red pepper flakes (optional)  
- 1/4 cup pasta water (reserved)  
- 1/4 cup grated parmesan (optional)  
- Handful fresh basil (optional)  

## Instructions

1. Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat.  

2. Add garlic and cook for 30–60 seconds until fragrant (do not brown).  

3. Add cherry tomatoes and salt. Cook for 6–8 minutes, stirring occasionally, until tomatoes soften.  

4. Gently press tomatoes with a spoon to burst and release juices.  

5. Add black pepper and red pepper flakes.  

6. Once the sauce becomes thick and jammy, add ~1/4 cup pasta water and stir to emulsify.  

7. Toss with cooked pasta until evenly coated.  

8. Finish with basil, parmesan, and a drizzle of olive oil.  

## Notes

- Sauce too thin → cook longer before adding pasta water  
- Sauce too thick → add more pasta water gradually  
- For deeper flavor → add 1 tbsp butter at the end  
- For more acidity → add a splash of white wine or lemon juice  
- Roasted variation: roast tomatoes at 425°F for 15–20 minutes before cooking  

## Tips

- Emulsification (fat + pasta water) is key for a silky, restaurant-quality sauce  
- Do not overcook garlic — it will turn bitter  
- Use high-quality olive oil for best flavor  
